    {"id": 7, "type": "manual", "slot": "(a) the vertex-form equation",
     "desc": "Part (a): the equation must be y = (x+3)^2 - 2. Full credit requires the plus sign inside the bracket for a shift to the left and the minus outside for a shift down; writing (x-3)^2 + 2 is the standard sign reversal and earns no credit for part (a), though part (b) may still be marked on the student's own equation.",
